2. Followed their [instructions to setup a local build](https://github.com/stm32-rs/stm32-rs?tab=readme-ov-file#generating-device-crates--building-locally), except I installed the [newest, unreleased version of svd2rust](https://github.com/rust-embedded/svd2rust/commits/master/). This has [changes for the relevant lint](https://github.com/rust-embedded/svd2rust/commit/19b8f360ce4b21bd0844b90bf2ccfadce6f8b63f).
3. Ran `cargo +stage1 check --features=stm32f405` in the `stm32f4` directory, and it was clean. 

I think [the code you tested](https://github.com/stm32-rs/stm32-rs-nightlies) is using the released `svd2rust` without the changes.

